{{Japanese name|Nakasone}}

'''Reo Nakasone''' (中曾根 玲央, ''Nakasone Reo''; born 15 September 1965) is a Sanese politician and a member of the [[Liberal Democratic Party (Okaiken)|Liberal Democratic Party]] (LDP) who has served in the [[House of Commoners of Okaiken|House of Commoners]] since 2015. He represents [[Ishijima 3rd District]], the same constituency held by his father, former Prime Minister [[Yasuhiro Nakasone]], for over 50 years.

A policy expert known for his deep knowledge of international relations, Nakasone currently serves as the Shadow Minister of Foreign Affairs under LDP leader [[Koichiro Sadanuma]]. He is a prominent figure in the party's moderate wing, advocating for a strong but pragmatic foreign policy that balances the alliance with [[Shayden]] and economic ties with [[Peilan]].

==Early life and education==
Reo Nakasone was born in [[Takasaki]], [[Gunma Prefecture]], the eldest son of Yasuhiro Nakasone. Growing up in a political household, he was exposed to high-level diplomacy from a young age. He attended [[Okami University]], graduating with a degree in International Relations in 1988.

Before entering politics, Nakasone worked for the [[Ministry of Foreign Affairs (Okaiken)|Ministry of Foreign Affairs]] as a career bureaucrat, serving in the Sanese embassies in [[Shayden]] and [[Adonia]]. This diplomatic experience earned him a reputation as a policy expert rather than a typical hereditary politician.

==Political career==
When his father, Yasuhiro Nakasone, announced his retirement in 2015 at the age of 84, Reo was chosen as his successor for the Ishijima 3rd District seat. He won the by-election comfortably and was re-elected in the 2016, 2021, and 2025 general elections.

===LDP Moderate===
In the Diet, Nakasone aligned himself with the LDP's moderate faction, distancing himself from the nationalist "Restoration" wing led by [[Toshiro Kurosawa]]. During the Kurosawa administration (2013–2016), Nakasone was a quiet critic of the Prime Minister's antagonistic stance toward neighboring countries, arguing that patriotism does not require provocation.

Following the LDP's collapse in 2016, Nakasone focused on rebuilding the party's policy platform. He became a close ally of Koichiro Sadanuma, sharing his vision of fiscal sanity and competent governance.

===Shadow Foreign Minister (2023–Present)===
After Sadanuma won the LDP leadership in 2023, he appointed Nakasone as Shadow Minister of Foreign Affairs. In this role, Nakasone has served as the LDP's primary critic of the PPO-OSP coalition's foreign policy. He has frequently argued that the government's weak standing on the international stage contributed to the collapse of the currency, stating that markets trust strength while the current government projects confusion.

Nakasone is a staunch defender of the [[Okaiken-Shayden Mutual Security Assistance Pact]]. He has fiercely criticized OSP leader [[Rento Nakayama]]'s anti-Shayden rhetoric, referring to it as a childish tantrum that endangers national survival. Regarding relations with Peilan, Nakasone advocates for a realistic engagement strategy, criticizing both the naive pacifism of the [[Sanese Communist Party|SCP]] and the reckless nationalism of the LDP's own far-right faction.

==Personal life==
Nakasone is married to Erika, a former journalist. They have two children. He is known for his calm, articulate speaking style, which contrasts sharply with the fiery populism of his political rivals.

